WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:01.701
Western intelligence shows

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:02.235
that Russia is

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:04.170
starting to gather aircraft

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.772
near its border with Ukraine.

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:07.841
This is an apparent attempt to bolster

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:08.675
the trouble

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:10.410
that it's having with the land defensive.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:11.311
Now they're trying to bolster it

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:12.879
with jets, with helicopters.

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:13.279
All of this

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:14.647
according to a new report

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:16.082
in the Financial Times.

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:17.217
All of this is also happening

00:00:17.217 --> 00:00:19.285
is the defense secretary, Lloyd Austin,

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:21.554
says Ukraine is expected to conduct

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:23.490
an offensive against Russia

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.458
in the coming months.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.061
And so

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:29.796
we believe that there will be

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:31.965
a window of opportunity

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:33.433
for them to exercise

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:36.302
initiative and then change.

00:00:37.404 --> 00:00:40.206
We'll continue to to

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:43.009
create the right conditions

00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:45.045
on the battlefield there.

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:46.746
Big questions about those conditions.

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:48.481
CNN's Fred Pleitgen is at the Division

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:50.550
Belorussian Border Crossing. Fred.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.885
As you're hearing these warnings

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:53.953
from the U.S., from other Western allies,

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:54.888
what more are you seeing

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:55.955
on the actual ground?

00:00:58.892 --> 00:00:59.359
There, Kaitlin?

00:00:59.359 --> 00:00:59.793
I can tell you

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:00.493
it certainly seems as though

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:01.828
the Ukrainians are extremely concerned

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:03.797
that there might be another invasion

00:01:03.797 --> 00:01:05.765
coming also from a territory of Belarus,

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:07.233
obviously involving Russian troops.

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:08.401
I want to show you what's going on here,

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:09.002
because we are in a

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:09.969
really remarkable place.

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:11.671
We're actually right on the border

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:13.473
between Belarus and Ukraine.

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:14.074
You can see here,

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:15.809
this is some barbed wire fence.

00:01:15.809 --> 00:01:17.977
This was put up by the Russians,

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:19.712
but only a couple of yards down the road

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:20.346
over there.

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:22.782
That is already Ukrainian territory.

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:24.551
And as you guys can see,

00:01:24.551 --> 00:01:25.852
it's heavily fortified.

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:27.887
There's several layers of barbed wire.

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:29.489
There's also some things

00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:30.457
that were put up,

00:01:30.457 --> 00:01:32.325
earth mounds to essentially stop

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:33.760
anyone from going through there.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:34.394
That border

00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:36.096
crossing on the Ukrainian side

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:37.363
is absolute utterly

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:39.132
barricaded from what we can see.

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:39.866
Now, we know that from the

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:40.567
Belarussian side,

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:41.301
this border crossing

00:01:41.301 --> 00:01:42.602
is actually still functioning.

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:44.070
From the Ukrainian side, it isn't.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.972
All the border crossings to Belarus

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:47.040
have been closed

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.007
because the Ukrainians

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:49.075
have that fear

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:50.076
that they could be attacked

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:52.112
from the territory of Belarus.

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:52.679
One of the things

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:53.513
that's also going on here

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:54.447
that I just want to point out,

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:55.648
Caitlin, is that there is actually

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:57.317
some international trolling

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:58.618
also going on here.

00:01:58.618 --> 00:02:00.053
If our camera operator,

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:00.854
our photojournalist

00:02:00.854 --> 00:02:02.789
Claudia, can try and zoom in on that,

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:03.223
you'll see there's

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:04.891
a Ukrainian flag there.

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:06.059
But the other flag next to

00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:07.494
that is actually the opposition

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:09.696
flag of the Belarussian opposition.

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:10.797
And I can tell you one thing,

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:11.664
the Belarussian authorities

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:12.465
are not happy about that.

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:12.665
In fact,

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:13.366
the border guys

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:14.968
that were around here with

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:17.270
they have called that a provocation

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:18.972
by the Ukrainians now.

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:20.039
We do have to point out

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:20.940
we're on an organized

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.009
press tour by the Russian government.

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:24.511
So we're a bit restricted

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:26.646
in our movement. Here in the country.

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:28.481
And we're on the north

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:29.883
western border crossing

00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:30.817
or one of the northwestern

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:31.718
border crossings.

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:32.519
And you

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:34.320
probably find more Russian forces,

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:34.888
for instance,

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:35.822
in the northeast

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:36.589
but nevertheless,

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:39.292
you can absolutely see the tension here

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:41.261
between Belarus in Ukraine,

00:02:41.261 --> 00:02:42.662
as Ukrainians obviously

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:43.897
bracing for a possible

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:45.064
another offensive by the Russians

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:45.865
and fearing

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:46.866
that there could be elements

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:47.901
launched from this country

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:48.902
here as well, Kaitlan.

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:50.370
Yeah, and given the role Belarus

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:51.804
played in the initial invasion

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:52.505
almost a year ago,

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.307
you can see why the Ukrainians feel

00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:54.841
that way.

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:56.476
Fred Pleitgen, fascinating report.

00:02:56.476 --> 00:02:56.910
Thank you.

